 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? That's usually the chain rubbing in the inner plate. You can squirt cooking oil on it, spin the chain for few minutes, and wipe it off. Yes, it's very cheap and works well. Just make sure it's clean first, so it doesn't leave grime behind. Hold the chain in a chain tool with the big gear on the left, not the cogs. Clean first. Damp cotton buds and a little soap will do it. A little. Just don't rub the chain dry, let it wipe around the plates a bit first.",
